  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">State of Palestine: Create Self-Employment Opportunities for Vulnerable and Marginalized groups in Gaza through Digital Channels (Go Digital)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project was designed to address urgent needs in Gaza, including high unemployment, poverty, and the impact of recurring hostilities. With over half the population below the poverty line and youth unemployment at 69%, the situation worsened further due to shifting humanitarian aid and escalating conflict. Initially, ITC aimed to support vulnerable youth through vocational training in digital skills, helping them access online income opportunities. However, following the outbreak of war in Gaza, the project was adapted to focus on developing e-learning materials&#x2014;enabling continued support for freelancers despite the challenging context, while staying aligned with the original objectives.

The project contributes to social stability by supporting employment and increasing the employability of the most vulnerable groups, including refugees and internally displaced people.</narrative>
  </description>
